  <section id="choices">
    <h2>10. Your choices and rights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Edit or delete your posts and comments, and choose which profile panels are public, at any time.</li>
      <li>In Camfrog rooms, <code>!incognito</code> / <code>!bridge hide</code> keep your name off the website. Incognito does more than that: see <a href="#incognito">Incognito</a> below.</li>
      <li>Choose who can see your cam on the website, or switch it off: see <a href="#livecams">Live cams</a>.</li>
      <% if (locals.memory) { %><li><b>Stop Pepe remembering what you tell him</b> (in rooms, on the mic, in PMs and DMs): see <a href="#memory">Pepe's memory</a> below.</li><% } %>
      <li><b>Make Pepe forget you</b> and delete your private conversations with him: see <a href="#forget">below</a>.</li>
      <%# mic retention: the download's choices (ops plan 8.6) and "Also delete my mic recordings" (8.5 B) only while the mic-recordings
          switch is on; the markers' sentence (8.5 A, as corrected by the third review: their only effect is on the next holder's OWN
          data download - micrec.ownSince / earlierHolder) always %>
      <li><b>Download your data</b> or <b>delete your account</b> in <a href="/settings/account">Settings → Account</a>.<% if (locals.micrec) { %> You choose what goes in besides your account: your chat logs (with your private messages with Pepe, both sides), your mic transcripts, what Pepe remembers about you, and your mic recordings. Pepe's part covers the Camfrog name linked to your account now, and only if no other PATV account had that name before you (Pepe can't yet tell their data from yours; your lines in pads' chat history under that name then start when it became yours); names you linked before aren't in it. In a room with more than one mic, a recording or transcript can hold other people who were on the mic at the same time. Pepe's replies can quote other people. What Pepe remembers leaves out who told him each thing, notes that name other chat members, and accounts an admin linked to yours. Recordings can be big, so one download holds up to about 256 MB of Pepe's part, newest recordings first; ask again with an earlier date for the rest (a download with a date holds only those older recordings). A download with Pepe's part needs your password or a recent sign-in, and we send you a notice when one is asked for.<% } %> A deleted account is closed after a 14-day grace period in which signing in cancels it; Pepe also forgets your Camfrog name<% if (locals.micrec) { %>, and if you tick <i>Also delete my mic recordings</i>, he deletes the recordings of your mic-ups (for every Camfrog name you linked, from the time it was yours; if another PATV account had that name before you, our team deletes yours by hand; a name you unlinked before 12 October 2026 isn't reached; one under a legal hold or an open report is kept until that ends; backup copies go within 7 days after)<% } %>. PATV keeps a scrambled marker of each Camfrog name a deleted account had (never the name itself), so the next person to link that name can't get what Pepe keeps of yours, or your lines under that name, in their own data download (see <a href="#retention">section 9</a>).</li>
      <li>Turn inbox notices on or off in your inbox settings; choose who can message you, block people and turn Camfrog alerts for messages on or off in your message settings.</li>
      <li>Clear cookies and local storage in your browser (you'll be signed out).</li>
      <li>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete or export your personal data, to object to or restrict some processing, and to complain to your data-protection authority. Email <a href="mailto:privacy@publicaccess.tv">privacy@publicaccess.tv</a> from the address on your account and we'll respond within the time the law requires. We may need to keep some data (for example safety records about content that was reported) where the law allows or requires.</li>
    </ul>
    <%# S1 V4 (ADR 0007 D16, OQ-20): ONE section for the chat hub ("PATV chat") and the pad chat archive (chatlog.js), shown only
        while the hub's erasure switch is on (accountdelete.privacyCopy; terms.js passes it). Its date is when the switch went on.
        O-20 (owner, 2026-10-24: V4 drafts, the owner approves the exact text in the PR): this revision of V4's draft adds how long
        each store keeps the lines and what "Download my data" includes. PATV chat's "no automatic deletion yet" is the hub's
        report-only purge in S1 (ADR 0007 D4, D16): change that sentence when the hub's purge is switched on. %>
    <% if (locals.hubErasure) { const HE = locals.hubErasure; %>
    <h3 id="delete-chat">Your chat lines when you delete your account</h3>
    <p>This covers <b>PATV chat</b> (the website's own chat on PATV's pads, such as the PATV Lounge) and pads' <% if (locals.chatlog) { %><a href="#chat-history">chat history</a><% } else { %>chat history<% } %>. When your account is deleted, what you said in public chat stays as the room's record: your messages in PATV chat are shown as a former member's, and you leave every PATV chat room; the lines you sent from the website in pads' chat history are shown as a former member's too, or, if you had a linked Camfrog name, under that name like your lines from Camfrog. They stay as long as the room keeps its chat: pads' chat history for the time in <a href="#retention">section 9</a>, and PATV chat until a message is deleted, because PATV chat doesn't delete old messages automatically yet.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Also remove my public messages:</b> if you tick it when you delete your account, the words of those messages are deleted too, in PATV chat and in pads' chat history alike (the lines you sent from the website, also those under a Camfrog name while it was linked to you, earlier ones included). You can ask for this once a day.</li>
      <li><b>What waits:</b> a message under a report is kept until 30 days after the report is decided (90 days at most while it isn't), and one under a legal hold until the hold ends; then its words are deleted.</li>
      <li><b>Not reached:</b> in pads' chat history, your lines from Camfrog and the lines you sent from the website while incognito with a linked Camfrog name (they are shown as "someone"); <i>Also hide my past public chat lines</i> leaves those out for everyone instead (see <a href="#forget">Make Pepe forget me</a>). Nor are lines under a Camfrog name you unlinked before 12 October 2026 (we have no record of it), or copies already sent to Camfrog or downloaded.</li>
      <li><b>Your copy:</b> <a href="/settings/account#data">Download my data</a> includes your lines in pads' chat history<% if (HE.export) { %>, and what PATV chat keeps about you, your messages there among it<% } %>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Deleted data may persist in backups until they expire (see section 9).</p>
    <% } %>
    <h3 id="incognito">Incognito</h3>
    <p>Incognito is a switch for your chat identity (your linked Camfrog name). It is off unless you turn it on. Turn it on or off with <code>!incognito on</code> / <code>!incognito off</code> in chat (in a room or a PM to Pepe), or in <a href="/settings/privacy">Settings → Privacy</a> on the website. Both change the same setting, and you get an inbox notice when it changes.</p>
    <p>While incognito is on:</p>
    <ul>
      <%# wave 3 (design §N.8, owner-approved 2026-10-28): with a Pepe that has the memory switch (locals.memory = memoryoptout.privacyCopy()),
          incognito is about the website only - N.8's bullet replaces the memory promise %>
      <% if (locals.memory) { %><li><b>Incognito changes what the website shows, not what Pepe remembers.</b> To stop Pepe remembering what you say, use <a href="#memory">"Pepe's memory"</a> below (or type <code>!remember off</code>).</li>
      <% } else { %><li><b>Pepe doesn't remember anything new you say</b> - in rooms, in PMs, in direct messages on the site or on Telegram. Lines that were still waiting to be remembered when you switched it on are discarded.</li><% } %>
      <li><b>You're "someone" on the website:</b> incognito hides <i>who</i> you are, not what you say. Your name, picture and looks are hidden on the live room view and in chat quotes; anything you say there may be shown or quoted without your name (as "someone"), never with it, and it doesn't turn up as mentions. To keep your lines off the website altogether, use <code>!bridge hide</code> as well.<% if (locals.chatlog) { %> The same goes for your lines in a pad's <a href="#chat-history">chat history</a>, its search and its downloads, earlier ones included.<% } %></li>
      <%# mic retention (ops plan 8.4, approved 2026-10-27): with the mic-recordings switch on, incognito doesn't change recordings (the
          owner's rule of 2026-10-27: incognito and !bridge hide are about the bridge, not what Pepe keeps) %>
      <% if (locals.micrec) { %><li><b>Captures of you are private:</b> snaps and clips that show you can't be kept or posted, your cam can't be used as a reference for AI pictures, and your mic audio isn't offered for clips. Your mic-ups are still recorded and kept like everyone's (see <a href="#mic-recordings">Mic recordings</a>): incognito is about what the website shows, not what Pepe keeps.</li><% } else { %>
      <li><b>Captures of you are private:</b> snaps and clips that show you can't be kept or posted, your cam can't be used as a reference for AI pictures, and Pepe doesn't keep your mic audio for clips.</li><% } %>
      <%# 1.99aft (review): true with or without the memory switch - Pepe counts no top word said while incognito (pepe_userstats) %>
      <li><b>You're left out of bounty evidence and analytics:</b> your lines are never quoted or sent to the AI judge when a bounty is checked, your most-used words aren't recorded for your profile analytics, and room statistics count you without naming you.</li>
      <%# WP-1 (section H, approved 2026-10-28): true today, not behind any switch %>
      <li><b>Your voice is still heard:</b> incognito and <code>!bridge hide</code> change what the website <i>shows</i>, not what it <i>plays</i>. If the pad has room audio on, website listeners and Pepe's live stream hear you like everyone else on the mic. The pad's owner can switch the audio off.</li>
    </ul>
    <%# 1.99aft (review): with the memory switch, incognito stops no memories - the paragraph says so instead of "it only stops new data" %>
    <% if (locals.memory) { %><p><b>What it doesn't do:</b> it doesn't change what Pepe remembers (that's <a href="#memory">Pepe's memory</a>), and it doesn't delete what Pepe or the site already stored about you, including chat logs, captures and analytics from before you switched it on.<% } else { %><p><b>What it doesn't do:</b> it only stops <i>new</i> data. It doesn't delete what Pepe or the site already stored about you, including memories, chat logs, captures and analytics from before you switched it on.<% } %> To delete Pepe's memories and your private conversations with him, use <a href="#forget">Make Pepe forget me</a>; for everything else, or to get a copy, use Settings → Account or email <a href="mailto:privacy@publicaccess.tv">privacy@publicaccess.tv</a> from the address on your account (see your rights above). Your points, games and commands work as usual while it's on.</p>
    <% if (locals.memory) { %>
    <%# wave 3 (design §N.8): the "Pepe's memory" text the owner approved on 2026-10-28 (aligned to the N.10 answers: the log commands and
        recordings unchanged, no migration). Shown only while Pepe's latest report has the memory switch (memoryoptout.capable), so it is
        never false whatever the deploy order. One word changed: "coins" -> "points" (PAT is points). %>
    <h3 id="memory">Pepe's memory</h3>
    <p>Pepe remembers things people tell him - in rooms, on the mic, in PMs and in direct messages on the site or on Telegram - so he can talk to you like someone who knows you. You can stop that at any time: switch off <b>"Let Pepe remember what I tell him"</b> in <a href="/settings/privacy#memory">Settings → Privacy</a>, or type <code>!remember off</code> in a Camfrog room or a PM to Pepe.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>From then on, Pepe learns nothing new from what you say.</b> No facts about you from chat, PMs or the mic. Nothing on your profile with him. Nothing worked out from your voice about other people or the room. What other people say about you isn't filed under your name, and his notes about a room call you "someone".</li>
      <li><b>He doesn't bring up what you said.</b> His answers, recaps, roasts and room notes leave your lines out. The room's log commands (<code>!log</code>, <code>!search</code>, <code>!replay</code>, <code>!seen</code>) aren't his memory: they look things up in the room's logs, so they still find your lines like everyone's.</li>
      <li><b>He still hears you in the moment.</b> He can answer what you just said, but he doesn't remember it.</li>
      <li><b>What stays:</b> the room's own logs of public chat, mic transcripts and mic recordings, kept for the room's usual time like everyone's, as its record; his logs of your PMs with him, until they expire or you ask him to forget you; your mic stats, levels, achievements and points (the room's games and boards); moderation records (kicks, bans, strikes); and the link between your Camfrog login and the names you show, which Pepe needs to keep your privacy settings working.</li>
      <li><b>The website is separate.</b> In a room connected to a PATV pad, what you say still shows on the pad - and can be quoted or clipped there - like everyone's. Incognito and <code>!bridge hide</code> change that, not this switch.</li>
      <li><b>What he already learned stays until you ask him to forget it.</b> Turning the switch off offers to wipe it too, and <a href="#forget">"Make Pepe forget me"</a> wipes it - with your private conversations with him - and keeps the switch off. (The room's public chat and transcript logs stay either way: they are the room's record.)</li>
      <li>This is separate from incognito and <code>!bridge hide</code>, which only change what the website shows about you. <code>!remember on</code> (from your own login) or the switch lets Pepe remember you again.</li>
    </ul>
    <% } %>
    <h3 id="forget">Make Pepe forget me</h3>
    <p>In <a href="/settings/privacy#forget">Settings → Privacy</a>, or with <code>!forgetme now</code> and then <code>!forgetme confirm</code> in Camfrog, you can make Pepe forget you. It deletes, and can't be undone:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>everything Pepe remembers about you: what he learned, your nicknames and linked names, and your mic history;</li>
      <li>your private conversations with him: Camfrog private messages, "Message Pepe" on the website (for both sides of the conversation) and the Telegram chat.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Camfrog private messages one of Pepe's admins sent you through him with <code>!msg</code> are the admin's messages, not your conversation with Pepe, so their copies on PATV stay: in your direct messages with that admin until you clear the conversation, or in <a href="#messages-camfrog-log">the admin's own Camfrog log</a>. To have your Camfrog name taken out of those logs, delete your PATV account or write to <a href="mailto:privacy@publicaccess.tv">privacy@publicaccess.tv</a>.</p>
    <p>It doesn't delete what you said in public rooms (chat, mic transcripts, snaps and clips), because that's the room's record and involves other people - unless you tick <i>Also hide my past public chat lines</i> on the website: then your past lines in pads' chat (under your linked Camfrog name, and the ones you sent from the website) are left out for everyone, for good, and your name is blanked in other people's lines (copies people already downloaded or quoted aren't reached). The same box is offered when you delete your account.<% if (locals.micrec) { %> It doesn't delete your mic recordings either; deleting your account can.<% } %> <% if (locals.memory) { %>It also keeps <a href="#memory">Pepe's memory</a> switched off from then on, so he doesn't start learning again - unless you say no when you're asked: untick <i>Keep it that way</i> on the website, or in Camfrog (where <code>!forgetme now</code> asks) type <code>!forgetme confirm remember</code>.<% } else { %>It doesn't switch on incognito, so Pepe starts learning again if you keep talking to him.<% } %> We keep a record that you asked (when, and how many messages were deleted), never what was said. Deleted data may persist in backups until they expire (see section 9).</p>
  </section>

  <section id="children">
    <h2>11. Children</h2>
    <p>PATV is for adults (18+). We don't knowingly collect data from anyone under 18; if we learn we have, we close the account and delete the data, except where we must keep it to report abuse.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="security">
    <h2>12. Security</h2>
    <p>Passwords are hashed, the site is served over HTTPS, sign-in cookies can't be read by page scripts, the most sensitive data is limited to administrators with every view logged, and identity keys are stored as salted hashes. No system is perfectly secure; if a breach affects you we'll tell you as the law requires.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="transfers">
    <h2>13. Where data is stored</h2>
    <p>Our servers are in the United States, and service providers such as Cloudflare may process data in other countries. Where the law requires, we use appropriate safeguards for these transfers.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2>14. Changes</h2>
    <p>We'll update this policy when what we do changes. The "Last updated" date at the top shows the latest version; for significant changes we'll also give notice on the site.</p>
